    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters 2026-06-23 with **Mickey Moniak** (74.96) and **Josh Naylor** (72.21) anchoring our offensive output. **Mickey Moniak** is our highest-rated asset today, fueled by a massive +14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Gray, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on a high-ceiling encounter with Keller, bolstered by wind blowing out and a strong +11% SP skill rating. **Corbin Carroll** (71.26) remains an elite start despite a modest park handicap, as his position in the three-hole and positive platoon splits against Leahy keep his daily efficiency well above the 70-threshold. Conversely, **Brice Turang** (64.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (62.92) provide solid middle-tier stability, with **Brice Turang**\u2019s move to the second spot in the order offering a significant efficiency lift that mitigates the threat of facing a tough arm like Lodolo.\n\nThe toughest decision on today\u2019s card was the exclusion of **Zach McKinstry** (52.58), who fell just shy of our starting threshold. While his platoon advantage against Rod\u00f3n offered potential, his projected efficiency simply could not supplant **Travis Bazzana** (54.93) or **Gabriel Moreno** (56.25), the latter of whom maintains value in the four-hole despite a mediocre SP matchup. We are closely monitoring the status of **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom**; both are currently penciled in with \"Lineup Pending\" tags and assume a lower-third and cleanup slot respectively. **Max Muncy** carries additional risk due to an elite catcher matchup that pressures his efficiency score. We will hold **Jose Caballero** and **Cole Young** on the bench for now, as their current platoon and order projections do not outweigh the day-to-day consistency provided by our starters. **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving no immediate room for further rotation maneuvers.",
